{"assets":["/statement-assets/1af403813c93b92a0c1bafc75d20c6d0fc45b68d5da6360349a660f721e912f3.png","/statement-assets/d8b20b7c04b9483ce13f76cd10e2457c318ccde251a7a204623872d4c8797e7f.png","/statement-assets/d9568306c0ae2db810ae218df0d5375926ad742b70bd2193e624e5cd5149672b.png","/statement-assets/0abdcb8dc0d33c6a0d7b361e702f504b8c7eaaae891f94a144e84ce1012b0951.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2207","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Where's My Water?"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3yV8PPnShSw"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Level 3 — David Luis Ortega, Where's My Water? "}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let $$$n, h$$$ be positive integers. Swampy the Alligator needs water for his bathtub, and you are tasked with getting it to him. Above his house, there is an $$$h \\times n$$$ grid of dirt and water tiles with $$$n$$$ columns numbered $$$1, \\ldots, n$$$. In column $$$i$$$, the bottom $$$a_i$$$ tiles are dirt, and the rest on top are water tiles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To get water to Swampy, you can place a drain on any tile that isn't a dirt tile. Placing a drain takes away all water tiles that can access the drain by moving only down, left, or right on the grid without crossing any dirt tiles."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, placing the drain on the $$$\\times$$$ in the grid below will drain both the top left and top right water tiles and result in $$$10$$$ tiles being drained:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/1af403813c93b92a0c1bafc75d20c6d0fc45b68d5da6360349a660f721e912f3.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is the maximum amount of water you can get to Swampy after placing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" drains? Note that water tiles that could have been taken by either drain are only counted once."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^3$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$h$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 2000, 1 \\leq h \\leq 10^9$$$) — the number of columns and height of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The next line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_i$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq h$$$) — the elevation of the dirt in column $$$i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2000$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the maximum number of water tiles that can be obtained with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"at most two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" drains."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n7 4\n1 3 1 2 3 1 1\n8 10\n7 5 1 3 2 5 6 8\n1 1\n1\n10 20\n5 2 1 2 1 3 6 7 1 1\n5 1000000000\n1 420420420 1 420420420 1\n1 1000000000\n1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n14\n43\n0\n170\n3738738738\n999999999\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the grid is the example shown in the statement. It is possible to drain $$$14$$$ tiles of water by placing the drains as shown:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d8b20b7c04b9483ce13f76cd10e2457c318ccde251a7a204623872d4c8797e7f.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the grid is shown below:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/d9568306c0ae2db810ae218df0d5375926ad742b70bd2193e624e5cd5149672b.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is possible to drain all $$$43$$$ tiles of water by placing the drains as shown:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0abdcb8dc0d33c6a0d7b361e702f504b8c7eaaae891f94a144e84ce1012b0951.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"table_cell"}],"kind":"table_row"}],"kind":"table_body"}],"kind":"table"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the grid is a single dirt tile, and no drains may be placed. So, the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2207C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2207/problem/C"}